config GICD_MISS_PPI_WAKE_REQ_WORKAROUND
	bool "Our own workaround for arm errata 1717652"
	default n
	help
	  Errata 1717652: Wake_request may not be delivered if multiple
	  cores are woken by PPI block at the same time.
	  1. Too hard to implement the workaround that arm suggested.
	     We must take an alternative way.
	  2. We can tolerate a one-time miss of a wakeup. But when there's
	     a miss of an IPI, the future IPIs with same type will be omitted
	     by software. See the cpumask_ipi for IPI_FUNCTION_CALL and
	     the need_resched flag check for IPI_RESCHEDULE.
	     So, we just implement workaround for IPI_FUNCTION_CALL and
	     IPI_RESCHEDULE, and do nothing for other SGIs or PPIs.

config SCHED_DFX
	bool "Yet another DFX_STATS, but default enabled"
	default n
	help
	  For long preempt-off.
	  The default threshold is for performance issues, not for stabilily
	  issues.
	  Better be disabled on FPGA for less bothering.

config LONG_IRQ_DFX
	bool "Dfx for long irq, default disabled"
	default n
	help
	  For long irq, including hrtimer handlers.
	  Since we can't rely on jiffies or hres_jiffies when a cpu got stuck
	  in irq-off context (likely all cpus are stuck), this feature must
	  bring overhead of ktime_get(). So we'd better disable it by default
	  and enable it by shell.

config LONG_IRQ_OFF_DFX
	bool "Dfx for long irq off by thread context, default enabled"
	default n
	help
	  There're two kinds of irq off: 1. disabling irq in thread context
	  2. an irq itself. A check in scheduler tick is helpful for 1 since
	  pending irqs will be handled when enabling irq or spin_unlock_irq-
	  restore. In this way we won't introduce any overhead so that it
	  can be default enabled similar to SCHED_DFX.
	  Note that this feature is not implemented.

config SCHED_PRIORITY_INVERSION_OPT
	bool "Help to resolve priority inversion caused by kernelspace locks"
	default n
	help
	  We temporarily apply a vruntime_offset for all cfs tasks (in cgroup
	  with this feature enabled) that are holding any kernel lock.
	  Conceptly it can be understood as assigning low latency_nice for
	  tasks in kernelspace critical section, in an extremly low overhead
	  way.
	  Note that for priority inversion issues the best solution is always
	  priority inheritance. This solution is to help when priority
	  inheritance can't work. For example it's hard and ugly to do PI for
	  rwsem and RCU. The main issue in the real world is critical tasks
	  blocking by kernel rwsem which is held by a background task.
	  So we treat all bg tasks holding any kernel lock prior to other bg
	  tasks, while not breaking fairness. And I think it's also ok if we
	  do that for tasks other than bg. But let's only enable bg now and
	  see if we need more work.

config SCHED_PI_DEBUG_LOCK_NESTING
	bool "Check if SCHED_PRIORITY_INVERSION_OPT can work correctly"
	default n
	depends on SCHED_PRIORITY_INVERSION_OPT
	help
	  By manually enabling sysctl_debug_lock_nesting (default disabled),
	  it will print log for unmatched critical_section_enter/exit().

config ENHANCED_CGROUP_RWSEM_PI_OPT
	bool "Enhanced priority inversion solution for cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem"
	default n
	depends on SCHED_PRIORITY_INVERSION_OPT
	depends on SCHED_VIP_PI
	help
	  The ciritical_section_enter/exit() is not good enough for the
	  cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem which is a bit special. This feature
	  simply boost all cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem holders to hisi vip,
	  with the support of vip low-overhead deferred boost interfaces.

config CGROUP_THDGROUP_RWSEM_OPT
	bool "cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem optimization"
	default n
	depends on SCHED_VIP_PI
	depends on !SCHED_PRIORITY_INVERSION_OPT
	help
	  if set, the thread holding the lock critical section will be set to VIP.

config CPU_MICROARCH_PERF_CTRL
	bool "Cpu microarch level control when we want more cap than max cap"
	default n

config CPU_MAX_PERF_REQ_LINK_MEM_TEMPORARY
	bool "Link memory max freq when critical"
	default n
	depends on CPU_MICROARCH_PERF_CTRL
	help
	  Don't use it. From any perspective this is what mips-mem must
	  have done well on its own.
	  And there shouldn't be any one link max memory freq though
	  mips-mem instead of pm_qos in devfreq.
	  In general I think,
	  1. Don't tell mips-mem, let mips-mem read it.
	  2. If have to do this in microarch perf ctrl, use pm_qos.
	  3. Most importantly I don't think we need to do this since we rarely
	     observe performance gap by it. Mips-mem has already done good
	     enough and we can also improve mips-mem itself in the future.
	  So just enable it on a single platform as a temporary solution.

